# Scotty, Chief Engineer: the same ability targets an opponent's creature too, but only a creature and only its
# controller's untapped artifact pays. On turn 3 an Island is not a legal target (the refusal) even though Memnite
# could tap. On turn 4 Bot1 taps both Moxen for mana, then beams Bot2's Grizzly Bears with Memnite (CR 602.2a); with
# every artifact of its own tapped the ability is gone (the second refusal) even though Bot2's Mox Ruby sits untapped,
# so only the controller's artifacts count. The Bears attacks unblockable and Scotty himself cannot block it
# (the third refusal, CR 509.1b): Bot1 falls to 18.

[Bot1 Deck]
Scotty, Chief Engineer
Island
Plains
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Memnite
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Ruby
Grizzly Bears
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Island x15

